# Leave unset both locally AND in production. Locally, the Vite dev server proxies /api
# to the local backend (see vite.config.js); in production, the root Dockerfile builds
# this frontend and copies it into the backend image, so the deployed app is served from
# the same origin as the API -- the relative '/api' default in api/client.js is correct
# in both cases.
#
# Only set this if you specifically deploy the frontend as its own separate service from
# the backend (not the setup this repo ships with) -- in that case it must be the exact
# URL of that separate backend service, including /api, e.g.:
#   VITE_API_URL=https://chronobooks-backend.up.railway.app/api
VITE_API_URL=
